%N A399630 a(n) is the smallest number m with exactly n divisors d whose first digit equals the last digit of m.
%F A399630 a(n) >= A005179(n). - _Michael S. Branicky_, Sep 06 2026
%e A399630 Of the 24 divisors of 672, five have their first digit equals to the last digit of 672: {2, 21, 24, 28, 224}, and there is no integer < 672 with 5 such divisors, hence a(5) = 672.
%t A399630 f[n_] := f[n] = DivisorSum[n, 1 &, IntegerDigits[#][[1]] == Mod[n, 10] &]; seq[max_] := TakeWhile[FirstPosition[Array[f, max], #] & /@ Range[0, 50] // Flatten, NumberQ]; seq[10^6] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 05 2026 *)
%o A399630 (PARI) a(n) = my(m=1); while(sumdiv(m, d, digits(d)[1] == m % 10) != n, m++); m; \\ _Michel Marcus_, Sep 06 2026
%o A399630 (Python)
%o A399630 from sympy import divisors
%o A399630 from itertools import count, islice
%o A399630 def f(n, t): return sum(1 for d in divisors(n, generator=True) if str(d)[0] == t)
%o A399630 def agen(): # generator of terms
%o A399630     adict, n = dict(), 0
%o A399630     for m in count(1):
%o A399630         v = f(m, str(m%10))
%o A399630         if v not in adict:
%o A399630             adict[v] = m
%o A399630             while n in adict:
%o A399630                 yield adict[n]
%o A399630                 n += 1
%o A399630 print(list(islice(agen(), 30))) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Sep 06 2026
